**Side-find, fixed (not just noted):** the FIRST live run returned n_dates_with_finra_data=0
of 69 attempted (looked like a dead data source) -- root-caused to FINRA's CDN returning
HTTP 403 Forbidden for Python's default `urllib.request` User-Agent string
("Python-urllib/3.x") specifically, while `curl` (browser-like UA) succeeds against the
IDENTICAL URL. One-line fix: `Request(url, headers={"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0"})`.
Strengthened the live smoke test to assert a REAL ratio for a known-valid trading day
(2026-07-17) instead of the weaker "None is acceptable" -- the weak version would have
silently passed through this exact bug. This is a reusable data-provenance note for any
OTHER prospector item that scrapes a raw CDN file without an API client library (e.g. other
"free CSV download" ideas in this same inbox) -- check for a UA-block before concluding a
free data source is broken/unreachable.

